From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:37:31 +1100
Subject: soc: apple: sep: leave the SEP off where the board keeps its mailbox
 disabled

With the profile picked by SoC alone, select() now also returns a profile
on boards whose device tree describes no usable enclave, and the warm
attach then enables the SEP node and its DART at module load. Most device
trees leave both disabled for that path, so their status cannot say
whether a board has an enclave.

The SEP mailbox's status does: the SEP cannot be reached without it, and
the device tree enables it (in the board file, or in the SoC .dtsi for
every board of that SoC) where the SEP is described for the machine.
enable_sep_and_dart() now leaves the SEP and its DART disabled when the
mailbox is disabled.

From the compiled DTBs of this tree: J773s (T6040), J575c (T6041), and
J714c, J716s, J775c, J775d, J873s, K114c, K114s and K116c (T6050) keep the
SEP mailbox disabled, so nothing is enabled or bound there. Every board
whose mailbox is enabled attaches as before.

The selection KUnit test also covers J773g, J815, K114s, J316s and J413,
and checks that SoCs without a profile (T6002, T6031, T8152) are refused.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>

[re-cut onto the K114s r3d tree]
